National Vulnerability Database (NVD)

pkg/cpe/cpemap.json.gz is generated from two NVD bulk feeds:

    https://nvd.nist.gov/feeds/json/cpe/2.0/nvdcpe-2.0.tar.gz
    https://nvd.nist.gov/feeds/json/cve/2.0/nvdcve-2.0-<year>.json.gz

It is a product-to-vendor mapping, distilled from the dictionary's live
application entries and from the vendor spellings cited by CVE applicability
criteria. The snapshot date of the dictionary feed is recorded in
pkg/cpe/snapshot_gen.go as NVDSnapshot, and the file is regenerated with
`go generate ./pkg/cpe/...`.

NVD data is produced by the National Institute of Standards and Technology
(NIST), an agency of the United States government. As a work of the U.S.
Government it is in the public domain and carries no redistribution
restriction. NIST does not endorse any product or service that uses this data.
